   "subject": "follow-up on adjust.methylC",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"EN-GB\" link=\"#0563C1\" vlink=\"#954F72\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">HI,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">This is a follow-up on how to do the adjust methylC when one has two files per individual: (5hmC+5mC and 5mC only).<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I wanted to have adjusted values for 5hmC since I don’t have a direct measurement for 5hmC.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">The following was suggested:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">“I think it would make sense to change the documentation at some point, you can use that function to get 5hmC levels if you have true 5mC levels.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">below I changed the arguments to more appropriate versions.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">The following will give you true_5mC if you have 5hmC+5mC  and true_5hmC<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background:#fafafa\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\">true_5mC</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">=</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\">adjust</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">.</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\">methylC</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">(</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\">mcANDhmc</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">,</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\">true_hmc</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">)</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">or to get true 5hmC levels from  5hmC+5mC  and true_5mC<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background:#fafafa\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\">true_5hmC</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">=</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\">adjust</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">.</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\">methylC</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">(</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\">mcANDhmc\r\n</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">,</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:black\"> true_mc</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666600\">)</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">the function adjusts methylated C counts in the object passed by first argument based on the second argument, First argument is basically should\r\n be 5mC+5hmC”<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">I made a methylkit input file where all positions in all samples have data and are ordered (these files work fine through the normal process).<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">So I followed the example provided at the end of the documentation for importing and reading the files:<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">hmc.file=system.file(&quot;pathtomyfile&quot;)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">mc.file=system.file(&quot;pathtomyfile&quot;)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">After which I got a failure for reading:<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">my5hmC=read(hmc.file,<a href=\"http://sample.id\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://sample.id&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234348687000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0iFys-UZHN8REqCnfELXWS\">sample.id</a>=&quot;hmc&quot;,assembly=&quot;hg19&quot;,header=FALSE,sep=&quot;\\t&quot;)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Error in .local(location, <a href=\"http://sample.id\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://sample.id&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234348687000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0iFys-UZHN8REqCnfELXWS\">sample.id</a>, assembly, pipeline, header, skip,  :<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">  , That file doesn&#39;t exist !!!<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">&gt; my5mC =read(mc.file,<a href=\"http://sample.id\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://sample.id&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234348687000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0iFys-UZHN8REqCnfELXWS\">sample.id</a>=&quot;mc&quot;,assembly=&quot;hg19&quot;,header=FALSE,sep=&quot;\\t&quot;)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Error in .local(location, <a href=\"http://sample.id\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://sample.id&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234348687000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0iFys-UZHN8REqCnfELXWS\">sample.id</a>, assembly, pipeline, header, skip,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">However, the files read without errors when using:<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">file.list=list(“pathtomyfile”)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Can someone explain why system.file must be used instead of file?<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">I am a little lost as my aim is to get 5hmC from the combined 5hmC+5mC file for the test and the control sample and unite the files just by\r\n the adjusted 5hmC files to do further analysis such as differential methylation.  I can already see that uniting will be an issue as you can’t have two\r\n</span>methylRawLists to unite.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Michelle<span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "CG36yR4iDJYJ",
