   "subject": "Re: follow-up on adjust.methylC",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div lang=\"EN-GB\" link=\"#0563C1\" vlink=\"#954F72\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">my5hmC=read(hmc.file,<a href=\"http://sample.id\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://sample.id&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234348696000&amp;usg=AOvVaw03QCrfkDIXgXUmxhMlfjed\">sample.id</a>=&quot;hmc&quot;,assembly=&quot;hg19&quot;,header=FALSE,sep=&quot;\\t&quot;)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Error in .local(location, <a href=\"http://sample.id\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://sample.id&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234348696000&amp;usg=AOvVaw03QCrfkDIXgXUmxhMlfjed\">sample.id</a>, assembly, pipeline, header, skip,  :</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">  , That file doesn&#39;t exist !!!</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">&gt; my5mC =read(mc.file,<a href=\"http://sample.id\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://sample.id&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234348696000&amp;usg=AOvVaw03QCrfkDIXgXUmxhMlfjed\">sample.id</a>=&quot;mc&quot;,assembly=&quot;hg19&quot;,header=FALSE,sep=&quot;\\t&quot;)</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">Error in .local(location, <a href=\"http://sample.id\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://sample.id&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234348696000&amp;usg=AOvVaw03QCrfkDIXgXUmxhMlfjed\">sample.id</a>, assembly, pipeline, header, skip,</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"> </span></p></div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>system.file() is used to get example files in the installation directory. This had been highlighted in the googlecode ebpage examples, there were also many similar questions in this forum, you should only use path to your files. so sth like the following should work to read the files one by one.</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Times New Roman&#39;,serif;font-size:16px;line-height:18px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:#000\">my5hmC</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">read</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;/path/to/file&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span></span><a href=\"http://sample.id/\" style=\"font-family:&#39;Times New Roman&#39;,serif;font-size:16px;line-height:18px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://sample.id/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234348696000&amp;usg=AOvVaw14ONF85-2Ig1T2qQVtNw0D\"><span style=\"color:#000\">sample</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">id</span></a><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Times New Roman&#39;,serif;font-size:16px;line-height:18px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;hmc&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">assembly</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;hg19&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">header</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span></span><span style=\"font-family:&#39;Times New Roman&#39;,serif;font-size:16px;line-height:18px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:#000\">FALSE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;\\t&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>after getting adjusted values, in your case you should get 5hmC values and obtain multiple methylRaw objects, you can make methylRawList as shown below:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"font-size:small;font-family:arial\"><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Monaco,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,monospace;font-size:12px;white-space:pre;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">myobj<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">new</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;methylRawList&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span>outList<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span>treatment<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span>treatment<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></span></code></div><br><b>outList</b> is a list of methyRaw objects.For example, list(obj1,obj2,obj3,obj3) will create a list of methylRaw objects provided obj1,2,3 and 4 are all methylRaw objects.<br></div><div style=\"font-size:small;font-family:arial\"><b>treatment</b> is the treatment vector you give when you are reading in the files. The order of treatment vector should correspond to the order of samples in the outList. This is similar to the treatment argument at read() function.</div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div lang=\"EN-GB\" link=\"#0563C1\" vlink=\"#954F72\"><div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:&#39;Times New Roman&#39;,serif\">I am a little lost as my aim is to get 5hmC from the combined 5hmC+5mC file for the test and the control sample and unite the files just by\r\n the adjusted 5hmC files to do further analysis such as differential methylation.  I can already see that uniting will be an issue as you can’t have two\r\n</span>methylRawLists to unite.<br></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"></p></div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>There will not be two methylRawLists to unite, there will be only one methylRawList containing only 5hmC values from multiple samples (tests and controls).</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Altuna</div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div lang=\"EN-GB\" link=\"#0563C1\" vlink=\"#954F72\"><div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n</blockquote></div>"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
